Title: Livingston Hall
Order: 20
Production Code: 1x20

INT. LIVINGSTON HALL - DIANTHE'S ROOM - NIGHT

AMB: wind against the windows, a low fire

Months earlier, in truth: [[Dianthe Lusk]], memory shattered a second time by the accident, is nursed by [[Aubrey Livingston]] in secret until, one day, he brings her a letter.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(gently, lying)
Reuel is dead, Dianthe.

Grief does what blackmail couldn't. She marries him.

Now, months into that marriage, she sits pale by the fire as he comes to her.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON (CONT'D)
You are ill. I'm told you see spirits. Do they wear the dress of African explorers?

DIANTHE LUSK
(flat)
At this very hour, in this room — a woman stood where you're standing. She wrote in the Bible and vanished, same as before.

He crosses to the book. Underlined: the same verse from Luke. Signed this time "Nina," not "Mira." He says nothing, kisses her hand, and leaves.

Alone, moonlight catches an envelope on the floor — African postmark. She opens it.

JIM TITUS'S LETTER (V.O.)
Master Aubrey — twice I have trapped Dr. Briggs, and he has escaped me. I shall not fail the third time. I have suppressed all letters, as ordered. Put the first payment toward the five thousand in my sister's account. — Jim Titus.

She spends the night reading every letter Reuel ever sent her, hidden in Aubrey's own desk.

DIANTHE LUSK
(to herself, hollow)
Reuel is living. And I am a bigamist. Made so by fraud, and worse than fraud.

Something cold and clear settles over her — a name, once heard, for a poison subtle enough to leave no trace.

DIANTHE LUSK (CONT'D)
For me there's no retreat.
